From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 01:31:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: carry calls with tgcalls-lite when the peer speaks
 tgcalls V2

Current Telegram clients run calls on tgcalls. The versions they register
are 2.7.7 and 5.0.0 (InstanceImpl) and 7.0.0 to 13.0.0 (InstanceV2Impl).
None of them is libtgvoip, so with library_versions left empty a call has
no engine both ends share.

tgcalls-lite (luneos-synergy-connectors, im/telegram/plugin/tgcalls-lite)
implements tgcalls V2 with signalling version 7.0.0:
- signalling packets encrypted as tgcalls' EncryptedConnection does and
  relayed by TDLib;
- ICE through libnice, using the STUN/TURN servers TDLib hands over;
- DTLS-SRTP and Opus;
- audio on the PulseAudio call devices libtgvoip already uses
  ("voipcall" and "webcall").

When it is built in (tgcalls_lite_INCLUDE_DIRS/_LIBRARIES):

- callProtocol.library_versions is ["7.0.0"];
- if the agreed protocol in callStateReady names 7.0.0, the call runs
  on tgcalls-lite. Its signalling goes out through sendCallSignalingData
  and comes in through updateNewCallSignalingData. Signalling that
  arrives before callStateReady is kept until the engine starts;
- otherwise the call stays on libtgvoip as before;
- LUNEOS_TELEGRAM_CALL_ENGINE=tgvoip in the service's environment turns
  tgcalls-lite off, for comparison.

Telegram's own reflectors (callServerTypeTelegramReflector) speak tgcalls'
ReflectorPort protocol, not TURN, so tgcalls-lite only uses the WebRTC
STUN/TURN servers. Calls are voice only: no video source or sink is wired
to the engine yet. The plug-in is built as C++17 when tgcalls-lite is
in, because its headers need it.

Also fixed: when a call could not be activated, the VoIPController was
deleted without Stop(), and libtgvoip aborts the process in that case.
It is now stopped first.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
